<article class="env-variant" id="02BQ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02BQ">Variant <span data-tag="02BQ">3.1.6.9</span> <span class="named">(The Homotopy Bicategory of Kan Complexes)</span>.</a> We define a strict bicategory $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ as follows: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The objects of $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ are Kan complexes. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $X$ and $Y$ are Kan complexes, then $\underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}} }(X,Y)$ is the fundamental groupoid of the Kan complex $\operatorname{Fun}(X,Y)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $X$, $Y$, and $Z$ are Kan complexes, then the composition law on $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ is given by 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \begin{eqnarray*}  \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}}( Y,Z) \times \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}}( X,Y) &amp;  = &amp;  \pi _{\leq 1}( \operatorname{Fun}(Y,Z) ) \times \pi _{\leq 1}( \operatorname{Fun}(X,Y) ) \\ &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \pi _{\leq 1}( \operatorname{Fun}(Y,Z) \times \operatorname{Fun}(X,Y) ) \\ &amp;  \xrightarrow {\circ } &amp;  \pi _{\leq 1}( \operatorname{Fun}(X,Z) ) \\ &amp;  = &amp;  \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}}( X, Z ). \end{eqnarray*}
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> We will refer to $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ as the <em>homotopy $2$-category of Kan complexes</em>. </p>
</article>
